/-!
# `keccaktree_keccak256_neon_x3` (AArch64, three nodes per batch, tail call) in place (`out == in`), for every count

GENERATED by lean/gen_inplace_arm.py; do not edit.

The access condition along the separate-region run (`access_all`), mirroring `All.all`: fewer than three
nodes (`cmp`, `b.cc`, the tail call: no memory); else the frame, the batches (a batch at node `m` loads
input words at or above `8m`, stores output words below `4m + 12`), the epilogue, `cbz`, `ret` or the tail
call.  The final bound is `4·(off + 3⌊c/3⌋)`; at the hand-over the next kernel starts at node
`off + 3⌊c/3⌋` (`LibArmAl.done_eq_of_x0`), whose message words are still in the buffer.
Flag-free segments: `Arm.accessRun_ann` with `annIP` (flags dirty except at `b.cc` and `b.cs`).
-/
